  "conclusions": [
    "The archived 88-byte event and terminal fingerprints are exact. The new classifier identifies the observed routing timeout without claiming to repair or diagnose the underlying network/service failure.",
    "Explicit connection/schema codes are distinguished; unknown errors, failed turns and malformed protocol remain terminal. No retry, budget, prompt, schema, evidence-binding or semantic acceptance rule was added or relaxed.",
    "The actual local Node supervisor, broker, ledger and session retain the first failure and unknown usage; a deliberate second local request is denied without a second transport dispatch.",
    "Top-level stop cause carries only symbolic codes, phase and reason fingerprint. Existing bounded/redacted diagnostics retain the original event; credentials and free-form request data are not added to the new cause.",
    "TC-R1 was independently reproduced and fixed: validated terminal ledger failure now survives later deadline, STOP and clock errors. Corrupt run/ledger identities remain rejected, and the clock is sampled after validation.",
    "All six changed integration expectations were inspected against their actual synthetic turn.failed fixtures. Their Electron matrices were not rerun in this task.",
    "Existing sealed runners and reviews were not resealed. The modified checkout rejects the old live entry before authorization consumption or process spawn; existing candidate and installed app remain frozen."
  ],
